            "review_title": "Review at La Falaise",
            "review_text": "SuzeeoutoftheCity201\nLondon, United Kingdom181 contributions\n0\nDelicious but bland fish meal\nApr 2017\nNow rebranded as 'The Cliff', this chic restaurant offers crazy-gorgeous sea views as well as an indoor restaurant and outdoor lounge for smoking, drinking and sushi. We had excellent wine and a mixture of sushi and main courses, all of which were faultless, though quite bland. While this isn't a criticism of the restaurant, it's more of a criticism of Tunisian dining places in general. Maybe it was my poor choices, but I never had the flavourful meals I was expecting from a North African Country. I ordered the salmon on a bed of black risotto, which arrives buttery, melting in my mouth, and - yes - bland. All in all, we loved the wine, the view and the great service, but a little lemon and seasoning wouldn't kill anyone.\nRead more\nWritten September 24, 2017",
            "rating": 4.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-11",
